Subject: [PATCH 3/3] notifs: dispatch after close-write or move, not attributes

An attribute event can arrive while the writer is still filling a new
notification file. The handler can then delete the partial record or
attempt a later dispatch after the file has disappeared. Watch for a
completed write or an atomic move instead. Keep delete events for the
notification-count hook.

The native real-inotify fixture reproduces the original partial-write
loss and checks delayed writes, the normal writer and atomic moves.
The desktop and hardware hooks are mocked in that regression fixture.

Based on sxmo-utils 303c755e88d2a25c01bdbc5b46aba1939318f839.
Unsent draft; no Signed-off-by is asserted.

--- a/scripts/core/sxmo_notifs.sh
+++ b/scripts/core/sxmo_notifs.sh
@@ -60,7 +60,7 @@
 
 	fifo="$(mktemp -u)"
 	mkfifo "$fifo"
-	inotifywait -mq -e attrib,move,delete,close_write "$SXMO_NOTIFDIR"  >> "$fifo" &
+	inotifywait -mq -e move,delete,close_write "$SXMO_NOTIFDIR"  >> "$fifo" &
 	inotif_pid=$!
 
 	finish() {
@@ -71,7 +71,7 @@
 	trap 'finish' TERM INT EXIT
 
 	while read -r notif_folder notif_type notif_file; do
-		if echo "$notif_type" | grep -qE "CREATE|MOVED_TO|ATTRIB|CLOSE_WRITE"; then
+		if echo "$notif_type" | grep -qE "MOVED_TO|CLOSE_WRITE"; then
 			_handle_new_notif_file "$notif_folder$notif_file"
 		fi
 		_notifications_hook
